    <div class="ambient-bg">
        <div class="blob blob-1"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
        
        <!-- Header -->
        <header>
            <a href="index.html" class="logo">LOTUS <span>NEXUS</span></a>
            <a href="index.html" class="back-link">← LANDING PAGE</a>
        </header>

        <!-- Privacy Content -->
        <main class="content-card">
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <div class="update-date">Effective Date: July 9, 2026</div>

            <p>
                Lotus Nexus values and asserts your right to civil liberties, offline privacy, and self-determination. This Privacy Policy details how data is managed within the Lotus Nexus application.
            </p>

            <h2>1. No Data Collection</h2>
            <p>
                We do not collect, monitor, track, store, or transmit any of your personal identification data, location details, metadata, or creative compositions. Lotus Nexus is a decentralized, standalone application.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Local Execution and Storage</h2>
            <p>
                All processes related to synthesis, loop playback, and composition generation run entirely on your local hardware:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Resonance Codes</strong>: Generated Base64 text codes are computed client-side using JavaScript, and are only copied to your device's clipboard at your explicit action. They are never sent to external servers.</li>
                <li><strong>Local Library</strong>: Custom compositions saved to your library are stored locally in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> or <code>IndexedDB</code>. Clearing your browser data will delete these files. We cannot access them.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. Zero Third-Party Integrations</h2>
            <p>
                Lotus Nexus does not integrate any third-party advertising, analytics scripts, social tracking tools, or external telemetry modules.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Standalone Portability</h2>
            <p>
                Because the app is built to execute offline without server communication, you can safely run it inside a closed network or download the standalone HTML client directly to your local drive for complete air-gapped security.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Since no backend accounts exist, there is no support dashboard. For questions regarding the code, inspect the public application source directly.
            </p>
        </main>

        <!-- Footer -->
        <footer>
            <p>&copy; 2026 Lotus Nexus & The Fluid Motion of the Future. All Rights Reserved.</p>
        </footer>

    </div>

</body>
</html>
